#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:548
msgid ""
"Aside from debugging, there is only one place where Litestar logs, which "
"is :class:`~litestar.middleware.logging.LoggingMiddleware`, which has been "
"changed to accept a logger directly. "
"``litestar.middleware.lgging.LoggingMiddlewareConfig`` has also been "
"removed, with ``LoggingMiddleware`` now accepting all configuration "
"arguments directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:554
msgid ""
"Users that have previously relied on Litestar to configure logging, can "
"simply use the standard logging configuration provided by their logging "
"library of choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:559
msgid ":doc:`/usage/logging`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:567
msgid ""
"Remove the default exception handler for all unhandled exceptions. Unhandled "
"exceptions will now be re-raised, for the server to handle. \"Unhandled "
"exceptions\" in this context means any exception for which no custom "
"exception handler exist, and that does not derive "
"from :exc:`LitestarException` or :exc:`HTTPException`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:575
msgid ""
"Your application's runtime behaviour won't change in terms of *if* "
"exceptions get handled. The main difference will be that, for an unhandled "
"exception, it will be the ASGI server that creates a ``500 - Internal Server "
"Error`` response, instead of Litestar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:602
msgid ""
"Remove all SQLAlchemy functionality from Litestar. Both "
"``litestar.contrib.sqlalchemy`` and ``litestar.plugins.sqlalchemy`` modules "
"have been completely removed. Users must now import directly from "
"``advanced_alchemy.extensions.litestar``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:606
msgid ""
"Migration: - ``from litestar.contrib.sqlalchemy import X`` → ``from "
"advanced_alchemy.extensions.litestar import X`` - ``from "
"litestar.plugins.sqlalchemy import Y`` → ``from "
"advanced_alchemy.extensions.litestar import Y``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:610
msgid ""
"This completes the separation of concerns, with advanced-alchemy being the "
"sole provider of SQLAlchemy integration for Litestar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:619
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated ``litestar.contrib.prometheus`` module. Code still "
"using imports from this module should switch to using "
"``litestar.plugins.prometheus``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:629
msgid ""
"Re-implement :class:`~litestar.testing.AsyncTestClient` to be async-native, "
"i.e. use the currently running event loop to run the application, instead of "
"running a separate event loop in a new thread. Additionally, a "
"new :class:`~litestar.testing.AsyncWebSocketTestSession` has been "
"introduced, providing an async testing utility for WebSockets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:634
msgid ""
"To ensure consisten behaviour across ``TestClient`` and ``AsyncTestClient``, "
"all testing utilities have been rewritten to be async first, with their "
"synchronous counterparts proxying calls to the async implementation, which "
"they run internally within a dedicated thread + event loop."
msgstr ""

